      "side": 1,
      "message": "The logic implemented by this method is quite complex and the method name isn\u0027t enough to suggest that logic.\n\nYou can either amend the method name or add a JavaDoc explaining how the message is computed.\n\nRenaming is my preferred option, suggested as an online edit.\n\nAlso, returning an actual `Optional\u003cString\u003e` is useful, as it would allow the caller to avoid if/then/else checking for emptiness.\n\n\n```suggestion\n    public Optional\u003cString\u003e quotaExceededByLowestAvailableTokensMessage() {\n```",
      "revId": "2a1a6bea4f6dcf3e9e18e307f21fc8b491fabff6",
      "serverId": "173816e5-2b9a-37c3-8a2e-48639d4f1153"
